rewritten-to-match
Same top-down merge sort. Slices become index ranges; the per-run clone becomes a copy into a second array, and the temp array lives in the state instead of being allocated per run. Stores are checked and undo-logged. The merge loops are bounded by the number of elements they can move (left..right + 1, and i..mid + 1 for the rest of the left half) where the reference loops until a condition fails; the conditions are the reference's, the bounds only let the compiler check the output index once per loop. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: t, tmp) is declared `unlogged`, kept out of the undo log.
